GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "9EF41060D62C998A"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aMissionEvents + {
    GC_Event "{D3A77B1A12F34AB9}" {
     m_sName "Timelimit (event 6, 4200s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{201A5B53026F7909}" {
      m_fDelay 4200
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{289307FE000D25E9}" {
       m_sTitle "Timelimit reached"
       m_sMessage "GM Discretion when to end the mission"
      }
     }
    }
   }
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{24886E7B1DB9691A}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Mission Overview:"
     m_sContent "Mission makers intent is to fill 1st Platoon first, and have 1st platoon be the main effort "\
     ""\
     "Unrest in the country has boiled over. Mujahideen fighters have taken over Kunar Abad by force, sending civilians fleeing from the city. With its close proximity to FOB Michigan, the US Marines is forced to respond in force."\
     ""\
     "US objective: Clear the city of enemy combatants and blow up any ammo storage crates found"\
     "MUJ Objective: Fight along AI blocking the US force from moving through the city"\
     ""\
     "This Mission does not have any hard end conditions. GM´s discretion (see mission notes)"\
     ""
    }
    GC_Briefing "{FDF737F696A8F1DA}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "METREP:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Date:</h2>"\
     "- 2009/08/01"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Light:</h2>"\
     "- First Light: 0645h"\
     "- Last Light: 1715h"\
     "- Time Now: 0700h"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Weather:</h2>"\
     "Clear and sunny with a light haze"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Forecast:</h2>"\
     "Weather is not expected to change"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Moonstate:</h2>"\
     "n/a"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Visibility:</h2>"\
     "Good with light haze around 2000 meters"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{09C6183E17FFC705}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "ENEMY"
     m_sContent "American forces have established a military base called FOB Michigan to the east of our position. The Americans operate with mechanised infantry, equipped with M16 rifles, machine guns, grenade launchers, and armoured HMMWVs. They have access to substantial ammunition and medical supplies."\
     ""\
     "The Americans wear desert camouflage uniforms and are well-trained soldiers. They will likely conduct a clearing operation through Kunar Abad once they realise we have taken the town. Expect them to move systematically, building by building, and they will not hesitate to use their superior firepower."\
     ""\
     "WARNING: American snipers have been observed in the hills surrounding the city. Many brothers have already been killed trying to move through open ground outside the city limits. Last night, our fighters attempted to lay anti-personnel mines in the northern tree line (marked in RED on the map). They were engaged by the enemy and forced to retreat. Only a very few mines were successfully placed."\
     "DO NOT leave the city - stay within the buildings and streets where their snipers cannot easily target you. The hills are a death trap."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3564E460A2D390D2}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "I. Situation:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Size, Activity, Location, Unit, Time, and Equipment (SALUTE)</b>"\
     ""\
     "Size: Estimated Company (+) sized element (approx. 80–120 fighters). Estimate based on multiple transport buses observed entering AO (Area of Operations)."\
     ""\
     "Activity: Enemy has seized KUNAR ABAD, established defensive strongpoints, and is currently conducting logistical resupply. Enemy is guarding a group of civilian hostages."\
     "During the night, overwatch elements engaged and repelled enemy fighters attempting to maneuver in the northern hills."\
     ""\
     "Location: Embedded In and around the town."\
     ""\
     "Unit: Mujahideen Fighters / Insurgents."\
     ""\
     "Time: As of 0500. Intelligence is less than 15 minutes old."\
     ""\
     "Equipment: Enemy dressed in standard Afghan civilian clothing; armed with Bolt Action rifles, AK-pattern rifles, machine guns, and limited anti-tank rocket launchers and anti-personnel mines."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Capabilities and Limitations (DRAW-DG)</b>"\
     ""\
     "Defend: YES. Enemy is dug in urban terrain. They will likely use buildings and civilians for cover."\
     ""\
     "Reinforce: POSSIBLE. If the buses left, they may return with more fighters, though current assessment is that the main force is already inside."\
     ""\
     "Attack: YES. Their goal is to stage an attack from this city. They have the capability to launch local counter-attacks against our entry."\
     ""\
     "Withdraw: UNLIKELY. Enemy appears determined to hold the logistics hub and hostages."\
     ""\
     "Delay: YES. May use snipers or skirmishers on outskirts to slow our advance. Enemy elements were observed carrying anti-personnel mines into the hills north of the city. While overwatch pushed them back, it is highly probable a minefield was established in the northern tree line (Area marked in RED on map). It is assessed as unlikely that mines are emplaced within the urban center itself."\
     ""\
     "Gas: NONE OBSERVED."\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Enemy’s Most Likely and Most Dangerous Courses of Action</b>"\
     ""\
     "Most Likely Course of Action (MLCOA): Enemy will retreat when met with overwhelming force"\
     ""\
     "Most Dangerous Course of Action (MDCOA): Enemy will stronghold buildings and fight to the last element"\
     ""\
     "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Higher’s Mission & Intent</b>"\
     ""\
     "Mission: "\
     "1st Battalion CLEARS the KUNAR Valley IOT deny enemy staging grounds and restore freedom of movement to the region."\
     ""\
     "Intent: "\
     "Purpose: Secure the population and disrupt enemy offensive capabilities."\
     "Endstate: All towns in sector cleared of insurgent forces; MSRs safe for civilian traffic."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Adjacent Units</b>"\
     "North: Bravo Company (1st Platoon) - Establishing Blocking Position grid 028-022"\
     "South: Bravo Company (2nd Platoon) - Establishing Blocking Position grid 035-030"\
     "West: None (Open terrain / Enemy territory)."\
     "East: FOB Michigan (Rear Area)."\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Supporting</b>"\
     "Recon Element: Currently in observation post (OP) overlooking KUNAR ABAD. Providing real-time intelligence."\
     ""\
     "Fires: None assigned. (Restrictive ROE due to civilians)."\
     ""\
     "<h2>C. Attachments/Detachment</h2>"\
     "<b>Attachments: None</b>"\
     ""\
     "<b>Detachments: 3rd Platoon.</b>"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A223673136771EE2}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "FRIENDLY FORCES"
     m_sContent "Our main force consists of approximately 250-300 fighters spread throughout Kunar Abad. Many brothers are positioned in defensive positions around key buildings and intersections. A group of civilian hostages are being held at the market near grid 0308-0275 - they are leverage and must be protected."\
     ""\
     "Another platoon has been assigned to guard the ammunition cache at the compound in grid 0324-0261."\
     ""\
     "Our transport buses that brought us from Asadabad and the Shuryak Valley have been positioned as roadblocks on the western approaches to deny the Americans easy entry."\
     ""\
     "Note: AI will be spawned in as blufor moves through the city."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{38863AEE06397829}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "II. Mission:"
     m_sContent "NLT 0500, Alpha Company CLEARS KUNAR ABAD, DESTROYS enemy caches, and ESTABLISHES Blocking Position to the West IOT DISRUPT enemy offensive operations."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{943C6C9DCFA4E52C}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "MISSION"
     m_sContent "Our platoon, along with our brother fighters throughout the city, will defend Kunar Abad and the ammunition cache for as long as possible. This position is critical - we are establishing a staging point for our planned assault on FOB Michigan. Every hour we hold this ground gives our commanders time to prepare the offensive."\
     ""\
     "The ammunition cache hidden in the city must not fall into American hands."\
     ""\
     "Mission makers note: DO NOT CHANGE WEAPONS unless you run out of ammo. Do not kill AIs to take their weapons."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B1BDECE302150645}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "As per Company Brief"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CA7B87BB6625680A}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "TASKS AND ORDERS"
     m_sContent "Your platoon is organised as:"\
     "- Racek-21: First fighter section"\
     "- Racek-22: Second fighter section"\
     "- Racek-23: Third fighter section"\
     ""\
     "Your responsibilities:"\
     "a) Defend Kunar Abad - STAY WITHIN THE CITY LIMITS"\
     "b) Maintain observation on American movements and report via the radioman"\
     "c) Coordinate with other fighter groups in the city when possible"\
     "d) Use the urban terrain to your advantage - buildings provide cover and ambush positions"\
     "e) Preserve fighter strength - withdraw and reposition when faced with overwhelming force rather than dying needlessly"\
     "f) DO NOT attempt to move into the hills - American snipers will kill you"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{6BCA2E3FF770535E}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "IV. Administration and Logistics:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Administration</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Enemy Prisoners of War (EPW):</b>"\
     ""\
     "Handling: Adhere to the 5 S's (Search, Silence, Segregate, Speed, Safeguard)."\
     "Collection: Any surrendered enemies are to be zip-tied and moved to the Company HQ location immediately. Do not leave them with the assaulting sections."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Casualty Evacuation:</b>"\
     "Self-aid immediately, drag serious wounds to Platoon HQ for the medic, and consolidate everyone at Company HQ once secure—we do not evacuate."\
     ""\
     "<h2>B. Logistics</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Supply (Beans, Bullets, & Batteries):</b>"\
     ""\
     "All personnel are issued a standard combat load and Individual IFAK."\
     ""\
     "Additional ammunition, smoke grenades, demolition blocks and medical supplies are available from vehicles."\
     ""\
     "Only medics may draw extra morphine injectors, saline solutions, epinephrine, and ammonium carbonate."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Transportation & Maintenance:</b>"\
     ""\
     "None"\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Communications & Pyrotechnics:</b>"\
     ""\
     "All units will maintain radio contact with higher headquarters and internal elements."\
     ""\
     "Signal flares and other pyrotechnics are issued as per SOP."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A85566F9B27745A1}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "SUPPORT"\
     ""
     m_sContent "We have no vehicle support. The buses cannot move from their blocking positions. No artillery or air support is available."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{51B516B80EF647F9}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Control:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Signal</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Radios:</b>"\
     ""\
     "All Squad Leaders (SL), Platoon Sergeants (PSG), Platoon Leaders (PL), Company Commander (CO) and the Company XO are equipped with AN/PRC-152A radios. (Dual channel)"\
     "Team Leaders are equipped with AN/PRC-343 PPR (Single channel)"\
     "Signalers are equipped with AN/PRC-119 (Dual chanel)"\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Radio Nets</b>"\
     ""\
     "/// PRR Nets:"\
     "Reference ingame “Group Menu” default keybind “P”"\
     ""\
     "/// LRR Net:"\
     "48.00Mhz - Company Net"\
     "47.00Mhz - 1st Platoon Net"\
     "49.00Mhz - 2nd Platoon Net"\
     ""\
     "<b>4. Recognition Signals</b>"\
     ""\
     "Green Smoke: Location of friendly forces"\
     ""\
     "Red Smoke: Location of enemy forces"\
     ""\
     "Yellow Smoke: Wounded or requesting aid"\
     ""\
     "White Smoke: Concealment"\
     ""\
     "<b>5. Challenge and Password</b>"\
     ""\
     "Challenge: CO SHOULD WRITE ON MAP"\
     ""\
     "Password: CO SHOULD WRITE ON MAP"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "RHS_USAF"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{EA4F6D404F2EE662}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "COMMAND AND SIGNALS"
     m_sContent "Only the radioman carries a radio (R-148). All communication with other sections must be through runners or face-to-face contact. Conserve radio batteries - only critical information should be transmitted."\
     ""\
     "Radio Net: 50.00MHz - Main Command Net"\
     ""\
     "Command"\
     "Overall command for the defence of Kunar Abad rests with the commanders at the ammunition cache compound (grid 0324-0261). Your section leaders will direct local tactics in your assigned sectors."\
     ""\
     "Chain of command:"\
     "- Section Leader (Racek-21)"\
     "- 1st Fighter Section (Racek-22)"\
     "- 2nd Fighter Section (Racek-22)"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{0A7B452449BE8322}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "WEATHER"
     m_sContent "Date: 2001/08/01"\
     "Time Now: 0700h (first light)"\
     "Weather: Clear and sunny with light haze"\
     "Visibility: Good, approximately 2000 metres"\
     "Temperature: Hot - conserve water"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{0E450A9C7A904B57}" {
     m_iOrder 14
     m_sTitle "FINAL GUIDANCE"
     m_sContent "Brothers, we fight for our land and our future. The Americans have superior equipment and training, but we have determination and knowledge of this ground. Use the buildings, use the narrow streets, make them pay for every metre. When they come in strength, fall back and regroup - live to fight again."\
     ""\
     "The hostages at the market are valuable. Do not let the Americans rescue them easily."\
     ""\
     "REMEMBER: Stay in the city. The hills belong to their snipers. Many good fighters have died learning this lesson - do not be the next."\
     ""\
     "Allah is with us. Fight with courage and cunning."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D18C1EA031E307BA}" {
     m_iOrder 15
     m_sTitle "VI. Mission notes:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Mission Intent</h2>"\
     "- US Force is expected to clear through every building in Kunar Abad. If Ammo Caches are located they are to be blown up."\
     "- MUJ Force is expected to survive for as long as possible causing problems for the US Force."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Setup timer</h2>"\
     "None"\
     ""\
     "<h2>JIP Teleport</h2>"\
     "Enabled for 5 min. After that - walk to friendlies"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Blufor Victory</h2>"\
     "Major Victory"\
     "1x Ammo cache destroyed"\
     "Company in blocking position towards Shan Kalay (034-025 and 034-026)"\
     ""\
     "Minor Victory"\
     "Company in blocking position towards Shan Kalay (034-025 and 034-026) but unable to locate the Ammo cache"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Blufor Defeat</h2>"\
     "90% casualties. A mesage will appear and GM is expected to call the mission if blufor is unable to accomplish the mission."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Timelimit of 70 min. A message will appear and GM can call</h2>"\
     ""\
     "GM is expected to call the mission. But should allow for firefights to end."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Game Mastering</h2>"\
     "AI may get stuck near buildings; Game Masters are authorized to reposition or spawn additional AI if the mission becomes too easy for the players."\
     ""\
     "Maintain balance and challenge, but ensure the mission remains fair and engaging."\
     ""\
     ""\
     "<h2>Mission by Perfk</h2>"\
     "Last updated: 2026-04-25"\
     ""
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
